{"id":"5aac35c319a7cbbe83a7495d4ea568b82627dcb5","axis":"silent","repo":"appwrite/appwrite","sha":"5aac35c319a7cbbe83a7495d4ea568b82627dcb5","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/ci/e2e.json","lines":["@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@","       \"packages/detector/\",","       \"packages/compression/\",","       \"packages/balancer/\",","+      \"composer.lock\",","       \"Dockerfile\",","       \".dockerignore\"","     ],"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Cargo.lock","lines":["@@ -960,6 +960,12 @@ version = \"0.5.0\""," source = \"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\""," checksum = \"2304e00983f87ffb38b55b444b5e3b60a884b5d30c0fca7d82fe33449bbe55ea\""," ","+[[package]]","+name = \"hex\"","+version = \"0.4.3\"","+source = \"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\"","+checksum = \"7f24254aa9a54b5c858eaee2f5bccdb46aaf0e486a595ed5fd8f86ba55232a70\"","+"," [[package]]"," name = \"hmac\""," version = \"0.13.0\"","@@ -2670,6 +2676,15 @@ dependencies = [","  \"zstd-safe\","," ]"," ","+[[package]]","+name = \"utopia-database\"","+version = \"0.1.0\"","+dependencies = [","+ \"getrandom 0.3.4\",","+ \"hex\",","+ \"php-std\",","+]","+"," [[package]]"," name = \"utopia-detector\""," version = \"0.1.0\"","@@ -2716,6 +2731,7 @@ dependencies = [","  \"utopia-auth\",","  \"utopia-balancer\",","  \"utopia-compression\",","+ \"utopia-database\",","  \"utopia-detector\",","  \"utopia-domains\",","  \"utopia-dsn\","],"additions":16,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ php-std = { path = \"crates/support/php-std\" }"," utopia-auth = { path = \"crates/utopia/auth\" }"," utopia-balancer = { path = \"crates/utopia/balancer\" }"," utopia-compression = { path = \"crates/utopia/compression\" }","+utopia-database = { path = \"crates/utopia/database\" }"," utopia-detector = { path = \"crates/utopia/detector\" }"," utopia-domains = { path = \"crates/utopia/domains\" }"," utopia-emails = { path = \"crates/utopia/emails\" }","@@ -52,6 +53,7 @@ cc = \"1\""," foldhash = \"0.2\""," getrandom = \"0.3\""," gost94 = \"0.10\"","+hex = \"0.4\""," hashbrown = { version = \"0.17\", default-features = false }"," icu_normalizer = { version = \"2.3\", default-features = false, features = [\"compiled_data\"] }"," icu_properties = { version = \"2.3\", default-features = false, features = [\"compiled_data\"] }"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ stacker.workspace = true"," utopia-auth.workspace = true"," utopia-balancer.workspace = true"," utopia-compression.workspace = true","+utopia-database.workspace = true"," utopia-detector.workspace = true"," utopia-domains.workspace = true"," utopia-dsn.workspace = true"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/README.md","lines":["@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@ utopia.libraries = \"validators,dsn,domains\""," |---------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|"," | `auth`        | `Utopia\\Auth\\Hash`, `Utopia\\Auth\\Hashes\\*`                                       |"," | `compression` | `Utopia\\Compression\\*`                                                           |","+| `database`    | `Utopia\\Database\\Id`, `Role`, `Permission`, `DateTime`                           |"," | `detector`    | `Utopia\\Detector\\*`                                                              |"," | `domains`     | `Utopia\\Domains\\Domain`                                                          |"," | `dsn`         | `Utopia\\DSN\\DSN`                                                                 |","@@ -111,7 +112,8 @@ of `packages/validators` and the password hashes of `packages/auth` are register"," `packages/validators/stubs/` and `packages/auth/stubs/` for PHPStan, which runs without the"," extension. A library that still has a PHP implementation is registered only when"," `_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES` names its package; today those are `detector`, `compression`,","-`query` and `balancer`. Otherwise Composer loads the package's PHP class as before:","+`query`, `balancer` and `database` (four classes of `utopia-php/database`, from `vendor/`). Otherwise","+Composer loads the package's PHP class as before:"," "," ```sh"," _APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES=<package>,<package>   # those packages' classes from the extension","@@ -311,6 +313,61 @@ Known differences from the PHP classes:"," - An exception thrown in a filter has no `array_filter()` or `getFilteredOptions()` frame in its","   trace, and an exception names the caller's file and line, since the classes have no PHP source."," ","+## Utopia\\Database: Id, Role, Permission and DateTime","+","+Over `crates/utopia/database` (the modules without I/O: `id`, `role`, `permission`, `datetime` and","+`error`), registered when `_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES` names `database`: `Utopia\\Database\\Id`,","+`Role`, `Permission` and `DateTime` of `utopia-php/database` 10.2 (in `vendor/`), so Composer never","+loads those four files. The rest of the package, `PermissionType` and `Utopia\\Database\\Exception`","+included, stays PHP. Off by default.","+","+Built by hand like the balancer, in `src/database.rs`: the same names, signatures, static methods,","+private promoted properties (`Role`'s `$role`, `$identifier` and `$dimension`, `Permission`'s","+`$role` and `$permission`), `Permission`'s private static `$aggregates` and `DateTime`'s protected","+static `$formatDb` and `$formatTz` and private constructor, so `==`, `clone`, `serialize()`,","+`var_dump()`, reflection and PHP subclasses behave as in PHP. `Role::parse()`,","+`Permission::parse()`, `Permission::aggregate()`, `Id::unique()` and `DateTime::setTimezone()`,","+`formatTz()` and `nowAfter()` are the crate's; a string that is not UTF-8 is read byte for byte.","+`aggregate()` takes `PermissionType` cases and throws the closure's `TypeError` for anything else,","+as PHP does. A `Role` subclass's getters, and a `\\DateTime` subclass's `format()` and `add()`, are","+called as PHP calls them. Errors are PHP's: `\\Exception` from `Role`, `Utopia\\Database\\Exception`","+(made with its constructor, so `$state` is set) from `Permission` and `DateTime`, wrapping PHP's own","+`DateMalformedStringException`.","+","+Where it is faster: `Permission::read(Role::any())` and the other types return an interned string","+for a role without identifier or dimension; a role object is read from its slots rather than","+through three getter calls and two new objects; `DateTime::format()` reads the `\\DateTime`'s fields","+in place and writes the 23 bytes itself; `now()` formats the clock in UTC without a `\\DateTime`.","+The crate's dates are UTC only: with another default timezone (`date_default_timezone_set()`), or","+`$formatDb` or `$formatTz` changed by a subclass, or for input the crate does not parse, the methods","+make the same `\\DateTime`, `\\DateTimeZone` and `\\DateInterval` calls the PHP class makes.","+`addSeconds()` always does, to change the caller's `\\DateTime` exactly as PHP's `add()` does.","+","+The package's own `IdTest`, `RoleTest`, `PermissionTest` and `DateTimeTest` run on the extension,","+and `tests/database.php` (6,779 cases) is identical on both: reflection of every class; `Id::custom()`","+and `Id::unique()` (length, hex, time order, uniqueness and spread of the padding, for 21 paddings","+and coercions); `Role::parse()` of 60 strings and every factory with 15 argument lists, `\"0\"`","+identifiers and dimensions, bytes that are not UTF-8; `Permission::parse()` of 56 strings and of","+3,000 seeded random ones, every type for 19 roles, `aggregate()` with `null`, `write` expansion,","+`$allowed` subsets, duplicates, keys, invalid strings, non-string elements and wrong `$allowed`;","+`var_dump()`, `serialize()`, `==`, `clone` and objects made without their constructor; PHP subclasses","+of `Role`, `Permission` and `\\DateTime`; `DateTime`'s methods over 45 strings, 13 dates, 14 second","+counts in 3 timezones, three default timezones, and its formats changed. The differences below are","+asserted at its end. Nothing in Appwrite or Cloud subclasses these classes.","+","+Known differences from the PHP classes:","+","+- An exception names the caller's file and line, and its trace has no frame inside the package,","+  since the classes have no PHP source; a `TypeError` for an element of `aggregate()`'s","+  `$permissions` does not say `called in .../Permission.php on line 184`.","+- `Permission::$aggregates` is declared, but `aggregate()` expands `write` as it is declared, even","+  if code bound to the class's scope changed it.","+- `Id::unique()` waits for the microsecond to change as `uniqid()` does, but keeps its own last","+  value: an `Id::unique()` and a direct `uniqid()` in the same microsecond can share their first 13","+  characters (the padding still differs).","+- A closure cannot be bound to the scope of an internal class: `Closure::bind()` into one warns","+  and returns `null`, where PHP's classes allowed it.","+"," ## Utopia\\DSN\\DSN"," "," Over `crates/utopia/dsn`, always registered. Its PHP package, `packages/dsn`, was removed once the"],"additions":58,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/bench/database.php","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@","+<?php","+","+// Times utopia-php/database's Id, Role, Permission and DateTime: `python3 crates/extension/bench/run.py crates/extension/bench/database.php . <utopia.so> 5`.","+","+require __DIR__ . '/../../../vendor/autoload.php';","+","+use Utopia\\Database\\DateTime;","+use Utopia\\Database\\Id;","+use Utopia\\Database\\Permission;","+use Utopia\\Database\\PermissionType;","+use Utopia\\Database\\Role;","+","+// A run meant for the extension that gets the PHP classes would time PHP against PHP.","+$internal = (new ReflectionClass(Role::class))->isInternal();","+$requested = in_array('database', array_map(trim(...), explode(',', getenv('_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES') ?: '')), true);","+if ($internal !== $requested) {","+    fwrite(STDERR, '_APP_EXTENSION_LIBRARIES ' . ($requested ? 'names' : 'does not name') . ' database, but the other implementation loaded' . PHP_EOL);","+    exit(1);","+}","+","+/** Nanoseconds per call of $run, the best of 7 batches of $n. */","+function measure(int $n, callable $run): float","+{","+    $run();","+    $best = INF;","+    for ($batch = 0; $batch < 7; $batch++) {","+        $start = hrtime(true);","+        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {","+            $run();","+        }","+        $best = min($best, (hrtime(true) - $start) / $n);","+    }","+","+    return $best;","+}","+","+date_default_timezone_set('UTC');","+","+$userId = '6564a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8';","+$role = Role::user($userId);","+$team = Role::team('team1', 'owner');","+$documentPermissions = [","+    'read(\"any\")',","+    'read(\"user:' . $userId . '\")',","+    'write(\"user:' . $userId . '\")',","+    'update(\"team:team1/owner\")',","+    'delete(\"label:vip\")',","+];","+$date = new \\DateTime('2024-01-02 03:04:05.678');","+$stored = '2024-01-02 03:04:05.678';","+","+$results = [","+    'Id::unique' => measure(20000, fn () => Id::unique()),","+    'Id::unique(0)' => measure(20000, fn () => Id::unique(0)),","+    'Id::custom' => measure(500000, fn () => Id::custom('custom-id')),","+    'Role::any' => measure(300000, fn () => Role::any()),","+    'Role::user' => measure(300000, fn () => Role::user($userId)),","+    'Role::team(id, dim)' => measure(300000, fn () => Role::team('team1', 'owner')),","+    'Role->toString' => measure(300000, fn () => $team->toString()),","+    'Role->getIdentifier' => measure(500000, fn () => $role->getIdentifier()),","+    'Role::parse' => measure(200000, fn () => Role::parse('team:team1/owner')),","+    'read(Role::any())' => measure(300000, fn () => Permission::read(Role::any())),","+    'read(Role::user($id))' => measure(300000, fn () => Permission::read(Role::user($userId))),","+    'update(team role)' => measure(300000, fn () => Permission::update($team)),","+    'Permission::parse' => measure(200000, fn () => Permission::parse('read(\"user:' . '6564a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8' . '\")')),","+    'Permission::parse dimension' => measure(200000, fn () => Permission::parse('update(\"team:team1/owner\")')),","+    'Permission->toString' => measure(300000, fn () => (new Permission('read', 'user', $userId))->toString()),","+    'aggregate(5)' => measure(50000, fn () => Permission::aggregate($documentPermissions)),","+    'aggregate(5, allowed)' => measure(50000, fn () => Permission::aggregate($documentPermissions, [PermissionType::Read, PermissionType::Update])),","+    'aggregate(null)' => measure(300000, fn () => Permission::aggregate(null)),","+    'DateTime::now' => measure(200000, fn () => DateTime::now()),","+    'DateTime::format' => measure(300000, fn () => DateTime::format($date)),","+    'DateTime::addSeconds' => measure(100000, fn () => DateTime::addSeconds(new \\DateTime(), 3600)),","+    'DateTime::formatTz' => measure(200000, fn () => DateTime::formatTz($stored)),","+    'DateTime::setTimezone' => measure(100000, fn () => DateTime::setTimezone('2024-01-02T03:04:05.678+02:00')),","+    'DateTime::nowAfter' => measure(100000, fn () => DateTime::nowAfter($stored)),","+];","+$results['peak memory MB'] = round(memory_get_peak_usage() / 1048576, 1);","+","+echo json_encode($results), PHP_EOL;"],"additions":80,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/src/balancer.rs","lines":["@@ -619,7 +619,7 @@ unsafe fn frozen_array(ht: *mut HashTable) -> Zval {"," "," /// Runs a body that calls no PHP code, a panic thrown as PHP's `Error`."," #[inline(always)]","-fn guard(body: impl FnOnce()) {","+pub(crate) fn guard(body: impl FnOnce()) {","     if let Err(payload) = std::panic::catch_unwind(AssertUnwindSafe(body)) {","         panicked(payload.as_ref());","     }","@@ -639,7 +639,7 @@ fn panicked(payload: &(dyn std::any::Any + Send)) {"," }"," "," /// Runs a body that calls PHP code under `zend_try` (`run_handler` without its thread-local bookkeeping).","-fn guard_engine<F: FnOnce()>(body: F) {","+pub(crate) fn guard_engine<F: FnOnce()>(body: F) {","     struct Frame<F> {","         body: std::mem::ManuallyDrop<F>,","         panic: Option<Box<dyn std::any::Any + Send>>,"],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/src/classes/engine.rs","lines":["@@ -145,6 +145,16 @@ impl Property {","     pub const fn new(name: &'static str) -> Self {","         Self { name, offset: AtomicU32::new(0) }","     }","+","+    /// The property's name.","+    pub fn name(&self) -> &'static str {","+        self.name","+    }","+","+    /// Records the offset of the property's slot, once declared.","+    pub fn set_offset(&self, offset: u32) {","+        self.offset.store(offset, Ordering::Release);","+    }"," }"," "," /// Declares `property` as a protected typed property of `class`, with `default`; `None`"],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/extension/src/database.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,1602 @@","+//! `Utopia\\Database\\Id`, `Role`, `Permission` and `DateTime` over [`utopia_database`], built by hand","+//! like the balancer (see the README). `PermissionType` and `Utopia\\Database\\Exception` stay the","+//! package's PHP classes.","+","+use std::borrow::Cow;","+use std::cell::Cell;","+use std::ffi::c_char;","+use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicPtr, Ordering};","+","+use ext_php_rs::args::ArgInfoTables;","+use ext_php_rs::boxed::ZBox;","+use ext_php_rs::convert::IntoZval;","+use ext_php_rs::exception::throw;","+use ext_php_rs::ffi::{zend_class_entry, zend_function, zend_object, zend_property_info, zend_string, zend_type, zval};","+use ext_php_rs::flags::{MethodFlags, PropertyFlags};","+use ext_php_rs::types::{ZendObject, ZendStr, Zval};","+use ext_php_rs::zend::{ClassEntry, ExecuteData, ExecutorGlobals, ce};","+use utopia_database::{Permission, PermissionType, Role, datetime, id};","+","+use crate::balancer::{guard, guard_engine};","+use crate::classes::engine::{","+    self, Callee, Literal, MAY_BE_ARRAY, MAY_BE_LONG, MAY_BE_NULL, MAY_BE_STRING, Property, too_few,","+};","+use crate::classes::leaf::{self, FunctionHandler, Method, PRIVATE, stored};","+","+const ID_NAME: &str = \"Utopia\\\\Database\\\\Id\";","+const ROLE_NAME: &str = \"Utopia\\\\Database\\\\Role\";","+const PERMISSION_NAME: &str = \"Utopia\\\\Database\\\\Permission\";","+const DATETIME_NAME: &str = \"Utopia\\\\Database\\\\DateTime\";","+const PERMISSION_TYPE_NAME: &str = \"Utopia\\\\Database\\\\PermissionType\";","+const EXCEPTION_NAME: &str = \"Utopia\\\\Database\\\\Exception\";","+","+static ROLE_CLASS: AtomicPtr<ClassEntry> = AtomicPtr::new(std::ptr::null_mut());","+static PERMISSION_CLASS: AtomicPtr<ClassEntry> = AtomicPtr::new(std::ptr::null_mut());","+static DATETIME_CLASS: AtomicPtr<ClassEntry> = AtomicPtr::new(std::ptr::null_mut());","+","+#[inline(always)]","+fn role_class() -> &'static ClassEntry {","+    stored(&ROLE_CLASS)","+}","+","+#[inline(always)]","+fn permission_class() -> &'static ClassEntry {","+    stored(&PERMISSION_CLASS)","+}","+","+// Role's properties, then Permission's.","+static ROLE: Property = Property::new(\"role\");","+static IDENTIFIER: Property = Property::new(\"identifier\");","+static DIMENSION: Property = Property::new(\"dimension\");","+static PERMISSION_ROLE: Property = Property::new(\"role\");","+static PERMISSION: Property = Property::new(\"permission\");","+","+static EMPTY: Literal = Literal::new(\"\");","+","+/// The role names the factories use, by [`ROLE_NAMES`] index.","+const ROLE_NAMES: [&str; 7] = [\"any\", \"guests\", \"users\", \"user\", \"team\", \"member\", \"label\"];","+static ROLE_LITERALS: [Literal; 7] = [","+    Literal::new(\"any\"),","+    Literal::new(\"guests\"),","+    Literal::new(\"users\"),","+    Literal::new(\"user\"),","+    Literal::new(\"team\"),","+    Literal::new(\"member\"),","+    Literal::new(\"label\"),","+];","+const ANY: usize = 0;","+const GUESTS: usize = 1;","+const USERS: usize = 2;","+const USER: usize = 3;","+const TEAM: usize = 4;","+const MEMBER: usize = 5;","+const LABEL: usize = 6;","+","+const TYPES: [PermissionType; 5] = [","+    PermissionType::Create,","+    PermissionType::Read,","+    PermissionType::Update,","+    PermissionType::Delete,","+    PermissionType::Write,","+];","+static TYPE_LITERALS: [Literal; 5] = [","+    Literal::new(\"create\"),","+    Literal::new(\"read\"),","+    Literal::new(\"update\"),","+    Literal::new(\"delete\"),","+    Literal::new(\"write\"),","+];","+","+macro_rules! permission_literals {","+    ($($kind:literal),*) => {","+        [$([","+            Literal::new(concat!($kind, \"(\\\"any\\\")\")),","+            Literal::new(concat!($kind, \"(\\\"guests\\\")\")),","+            Literal::new(concat!($kind, \"(\\\"users\\\")\")),","+            Literal::new(concat!($kind, \"(\\\"user\\\")\")),","+            Literal::new(concat!($kind, \"(\\\"team\\\")\")),","+            Literal::new(concat!($kind, \"(\\\"member\\\")\")),","+            Literal::new(concat!($kind, \"(\\\"label\\\")\")),","+        ]),*]","+    };","+}","+","+/// `type(\"name\")` for every type and role name: what `Permission::read(Role::any())` returns.","+static PERMISSION_LITERALS: [[Literal; 7]; 5] = permission_literals!(\"create\", \"read\", \"update\", \"delete\", \"write\");","+","+static FORMAT_DB: Literal = Literal::new(datetime::FORMAT_DB);","+static FORMAT_TZ: Literal = Literal::new(datetime::FORMAT_TZ);","+static ONE_MILLISECOND: Literal = Literal::new(\"+1 millisecond\");","+","+static GET_ROLE: Callee = Callee::new(\"getRole\");","+static GET_IDENTIFIER: Callee = Callee::new(\"getIdentifier\");","+static GET_DIMENSION: Callee = Callee::new(\"getDimension\");","+static TO_STRING: Callee = Callee::new(\"toString\");","+static FORMAT: Callee = Callee::new(\"format\");","+static ADD: Callee = Callee::new(\"add\");","+static MODIFY: Callee = Callee::new(\"modify\");","+static SET_TIMEZONE: Callee = Callee::new(\"setTimezone\");","+static GET_MESSAGE: Callee = Callee::new(\"getMessage\");","+static GET_CODE: Callee = Callee::new(\"getCode\");","+","+unsafe extern \"C\" {","+    fn zend_declare_typed_property(","+        ce: *mut zend_class_entry,","+        name: *mut zend_string,","+        property: *mut zval,","+        access_type: i32,","+        doc_comment: *mut zend_string,","+        ty: zend_type,","+    ) -> *mut zend_property_info;","+    fn zend_std_get_static_property(ce: *mut zend_class_entry, name: *mut zend_string, kind: i32) -> *mut zval;","+    fn zend_throw_exception_object(exception: *mut zval);","+    fn zend_compare(op1: *mut zval, op2: *mut zval) -> i32;","+    fn zend_lookup_class_ex(name: *mut zend_string, key: *mut zend_string, flags: u32) -> *mut zend_class_entry;","+    fn php_date_get_date_ce() -> *mut zend_class_entry;","+    fn php_date_get_timezone_ce() -> *mut zend_class_entry;","+    fn php_date_get_interval_ce() -> *mut zend_class_entry;","+    fn get_timezone_info() -> *mut *const c_char;","+}","+","+const IS_STRING: u32 = 6;","+/// `IS_STRING_EX`.","+const IS_STRING_EX: u32 = IS_STRING | (1 << 8);","+/// `GC_STRING`.","+const GC_STRING: u32 = IS_STRING | (1 << 4);","+/// `ZEND_ACC_PROMOTED`.","+const ACC_PROMOTED: i32 = 1 << 8;","+/// `BP_VAR_R`.","+const BP_VAR_R: i32 = 0;","+","+// Strings ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------","+","+/// A PHP string of `parts`, concatenated into one allocation of the exact size.","+fn concat(parts: &[&[u8]]) -> Zval {","+    let length: usize = parts.iter().map(|part| part.len()).sum();","+    let mut zval = Zval::new();","+    if length == 0 {","+        EMPTY.set(&mut zval);","+        return zval;","+    }","+    let header = std::mem::offset_of!(zend_string, val);","+    let layout = std::alloc::Layout::from_size_align(header + length + 1, 8).expect(\"string layout\");","+    let string = ext_php_rs::alloc::emalloc(layout).cast::<zend_string>();","+    // SAFETY: a new allocation of the string's size, initialized as `zend_string_alloc()` does,","+    // then filled with exactly `length` bytes and the NUL.","+    unsafe {","+        (*string).gc.refcount = 1;","+        (*string).gc.u.type_info = GC_STRING;","+        (*string).h = 0;","+        (*string).len = length;","+        let mut at = std::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*string).val).cast::<u8>();","+        for part in parts {","+            std::ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(part.as_ptr(), at, part.len());","+            at = at.add(part.len());","+        }","+        *at = 0;","+        zval.value.str_ = string;","+        zval.u1.type_info = IS_STRING_EX;","+    }","+    zval","+}","+","+/// A PHP string of `bytes`; the interned `''` when empty.","+fn string(bytes: &[u8]) -> Zval {","+    if bytes.is_empty() { EMPTY.zval() } else { engine::string(bytes) }","+}","+","+/// The bytes of a string zval (empty for anything else).","+#[inline(always)]","+fn bytes(value: &Zval) -> &[u8] {","+    value.dereference().zend_str().map_or(&[], ZendStr::as_bytes)","+}","+","+/// PHP truthiness of a string.","+#[inline(always)]","+fn truthy(bytes: &[u8]) -> bool {","+    !(bytes.is_empty() || bytes == b\"0\")","+}","+","+/// A PHP string as the crate's text: itself when it is UTF-8, otherwise each byte as the","+/// character of the same number, which keeps every ASCII separator in place and maps back.","+fn text(bytes: &[u8]) -> (Cow<'_, str>, bool) {","+    match std::str::from_utf8(bytes) {","+        Ok(text) => (Cow::Borrowed(text), false),","+        Err(_) => (Cow::Owned(bytes.iter().map(|&b| char::from(b)).collect()), true),","+    }","+}","+","+/// The bytes of a text [`text`] made, mapped back when it was mapped.","+fn untext(text: &str, mapped: bool) -> Cow<'_, [u8]> {","+    if mapped {","+        Cow::Owned(text.chars().map(|c| u8::try_from(u32::from(c)).unwrap_or(b'?')).collect(